# Code Development Conventions

> **Reference**: See [vision.md](./vision.md) for complete technical vision and architecture.

## Core Rules

### Simplicity First
- Choose the simplest solution that works
- Avoid over-engineering or abstract patterns
- Prefer explicit code over clever abstractions
- If it works and is readable, it's good enough

### Code Quality
- **Readability over cleverness**: Code should be self-documenting
- **Single responsibility**: Each function/class does one thing
- **Flat structure**: Avoid deep nesting (max 3-4 levels)
- **Minimal dependencies**: Only add libraries when absolutely necessary

### Naming Conventions
- Use descriptive, clear names
- Functions: verb phrases (`get_embeddings`, `retrieve_segments`)
- Variables: noun phrases (`user_question`, `top_segments`)
- Classes: nouns (`RAGSystem`, `GraphBuilder`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (`MAX_TOKENS`, `TOP_K`)

### Code Organization
- Keep functions small and focused (50 lines or less when possible)
- Group related functions in modules
- Use `utils/` for reusable helper functions
- Import from `config.py` for all settings

### Error Handling
- Use simple try/except blocks
- Log errors with context
- Fail gracefully with user-friendly messages
- No complex retry logic (1 retry max for API calls)

### Documentation
- Use docstrings for functions/classes (one-line is fine for simple functions)
- Comments only when code intent is not obvious
- Keep README.md updated with setup instructions

### Testing Approach
- Test critical paths (RAG retrieval, LLM calls)
- Use simple assertions
- No complex test frameworks for MVP

### Dependencies
- Prefer standard library when possible
- Use open source libraries (except OpenAI API)
- Pin versions in `requirements.txt`
- Document why each dependency is needed

## Project-Specific Rules

### File Structure
- Follow the structure defined in [vision.md](./vision.md#project-structure)
- Keep `app.py` as the main Streamlit entry point
- Put logic in `src/` modules
- Utilities in `utils/`

### Configuration
- All settings in `config.py` (import, don't duplicate)
- API keys in `.env` only
- No hardcoded values

### Logging
- Use Python `logging` module
- Console output only
- Log: LLM calls, retrievals, errors
- Format: `[TIMESTAMP] LEVEL: Message`

### Data Handling
- Load data at startup (see [vision.md](./vision.md#workflows))
- Use in-memory structures (NetworkX, FAISS/ChromaDB)
- No database for MVP

## Code Review Checklist

Before submitting code, ensure:
- [ ] Code is simple and readable
- [ ] Functions have single responsibility
- [ ] No unnecessary dependencies added
- [ ] Error handling is simple and appropriate
- [ ] Logging is in place for key operations
- [ ] Configuration values come from `config.py`
- [ ] Follows project structure from vision.md

